{\H2x;\L\C4;GENERAL NOTES:\P\A1;\H0.5x;\l\C0;\P\pxi-3,l3,t2,3;1.^IALL DIMENSIONS ARE IN mm, ALL LEVELS ARE IN m.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;2.^ITHIS DRAWING IS TO BE READ IN CONJUNCTION WITH ALL PROJECT RELEVANT SPEEDECK LTD DRAWINGS AND CALCULATIONS.
  3
\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;3.^IALL SLAB PENETRATIONS TO BE CHECKED AND AGREED ON SITE PRIOR TO POUR.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;4.^ITHIS DRAWING SHOULD  NOT BE USED FOR SETTING OUT OF ANY EXISTING OR PROPOSED INCOMING AND OUTGOING BELOW GROUND DRAIN
  3
AGE AND SERVICES. LOCATION OF ALL EXISTING BELOW GROUND DRAINAGE AND SERVICES SHOULD BE DETERMINED ON SITE PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION.\C256;\P\pi0,l0,tz;\A0;\C7;\P\A1;\H2x;\L\C4;SLAB NOTES:\H0.5x;\C7;\P\l\P\C7;\C7;\pi-3,l3,t2,3;6.^ISLAB AREA =\C7; 161.73 [
  3
m{\H0.7x;\S2^  ;}]\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\C7;\C7;\pi-3,l3,t2,3;7.^ISLAB PERIMETER =\C7; 53.96 [m]\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\C7;\C7;\pi-3,l3,t2,3;8.^ISLAB THICKNESS  =\C7; 225 [mm] U.N.O.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\C7;\C7;\pi-3,l3,t2,3;\H0.99998x;9.^ICONCRETE VOLUME =\C7; 36.39 [m{\H0.
  3
7x;\S3^  ;}]\P\pi0,l0,tz;\H0.99998x;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;10.^ICONCRETE TO BE DESIGNATED MIX RC28/35 BY QA ACCREDITED CONCRETE SUPPLIER HOLDING EITHER QSRMC OR BSI KITEMARK CERTIFICATE.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\A1;\H2x;\L\C4;PILE NOTES:\l\C256;\P\H0.5x;\C7;\P\pi-3,l3,
  3
t2,3;\H0.99994x;11.^IPILES ARE: \H1.0001x;300Ø SFA\H0.99997x;\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\H2x;\L\C4;REINFORCEMENT NOTES:\P\H0.5x;\l\C7;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;\H0.99987x;\C0;12.^INOMINAL COVER TO REINFORCEMENT:\P\pi1,tz;\A0;TOP - 35mm U.N.O. \PBOTTOM - 40mm ^I\PSIDE - 40mm 
  3
\A1;\P\pi0,l0;\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;13.^ISTANDARD LAP LENGTHS ARE:\P\pi4,l0,tz;H10 - 400 mm\PH12 - 500 mm\P\A0;H16 - 650 mm\P\P\pi-3,l3,t2,3;\A1;\H1.0001x;14.^IMAXIMUM SPACING OF REINFORCEMENT SHALL NOT EXCEED 250mm FOR PRINCIPAL AND 400mm FOR SECONDARY REBA
  3
RS, IN ACCORDANCE WITH SECTION 9.3.1.1 (3) FROM BS EN 1992-1-1:2004. WHERE SPACING BETWEEN TWO ADJACENT BARS EXCEEDS 200mm BUT IS LESS THAN 250mm, PLEASE ENSURE MINIMUM 5NO REBARS ARE DEPLOYED IN A GIVEN 1.0m WIDE STRIP U.N.O. IF SPACING BETWEEN PRIN
  3
